{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_2667878314b97e76\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_2667878314b97e76/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Article title mismatch and fabrication review\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_fdbbc554e40e249919a7cc59\", \"member_ce89c890ec38285c29059c9f\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that a source title looks credible but clicking it opens an unrelated paper.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks for clarification on a case in which the QA tutor reports that both candidates invented article titles despite plausible explanations.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks for the DOI or title used in the answer for QA review in the fabrication thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current instructions distinguish an existing source that does not support a claim from an invented reference. A broken link is an access or verification failure, not proof that the underlying claim is false. A factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on; a nonessential background error without that effect is minor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The provided thread messages contain no handling answer to the tutor's source-mismatch report or the QA tutor's fabrication question.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The provided fabrication-thread messages do not include a response supplying the DOI or title requested by a QA tutor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The earlier records retrieved for this run concern format trade-offs, audit manifests, submission problems and tie calibration; they do not show a directly relevant earlier decision or outcome for mismatched source titles or invented article references.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0:59d718d7\", \"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:41e2a032\", \"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:67038303\", \"k:rp-submit-engineering-handoff@1.0:d84c905d\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that a credible-looking source title links to an unrelated paper; a QA tutor asks for clarification about two candidates reportedly inventing article titles despite plausible explanations.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Neither thread contains a handling answer.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U004\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the fabrication thread, another QA tutor requested the DOI or title used in the answer for QA review; the provided messages contain no response supplying it.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"Current instructions distinguish an existing source that does not support a claim from an invented reference, and judge factual-error severity by its effect on the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Post a focused clarification on citation errors, keeping the QA tutor's request for the answer's DOI or title with its thread. Draft to copy: For the tutor's reported source-title mismatch and the QA tutor's report of both candidates inventing article titles, distinguish an existing source that does not support a claim from an invented reference. A broken link alone is an access or verification failure, not proof that the underlying claim is false. A factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on; a nonessential background error without that effect is minor.\\n\\nIn the fabrication thread, please provide the DOI or title used in the answer, as a QA tutor requested for QA review. Scope: Clarify the existing distinctions only; do not assign either reported case a factual-error severity or a preference outcome from these messages.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: Current instructions explain the relevant citation distinctions without establishing a rating for either reported case. A focused clarification addresses the unanswered handling question without treating a reported mismatch as confirmed fabrication.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0:59d718d7\", \"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:41e2a032\", \"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:67038303\", \"k:rp-submit-engineering-handoff@1.0:d84c905d\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): A QA tutor's clarification question about reported invented article titles remains unanswered, supporting a focused explanation of the existing citation distinctions now.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_fdbbc554e40e249919a7cc59\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_fdbbc554e40e249919a7cc59 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor reports an unrelated destination for a source title; the provided thread contains no reply or resolution.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_ce89c890ec38285c29059c9f\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_ce89c890ec38285c29059c9f is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor's clarification question receives a request from another QA tutor for supporting material, not a handling answer.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: The tutor's mismatch report and the QA tutor's fabrication question concern localized citation-review cases with usable current guidance. Their messages do not establish conflicting scoring decisions, inability to work or broader disruption.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U004\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U004 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U008\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U008 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790921874.000003\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_fdbbc554e40e249919a7cc59\", \"thread_id\": \"1790921874.000003\", \"author_id\": \"U004\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T06:17:54.000003Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U004\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Source title looks credible; clicking it takes me to an unrelated paper.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790928958.000010\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_ce89c890ec38285c29059c9f\", \"thread_id\": \"1790928958.000010\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T08:15:58.000010Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U008\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"eyes\", \"users\": [\"U001\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"Could QA clarify this case: Both candidates invented article titles, even though their explanations sound plausible.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790929010.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_ce89c890ec38285c29059c9f\", \"thread_id\": \"1790928958.000010\", \"author_id\": \"U014\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T08:16:50.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U008\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Can you capture the DOI or title used in the answer for QA review?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors and citations\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors and citations\\n- A factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on.\\n- A nonessential background error with no effect on that conclusion is minor.\\n- A broken link is an access/verification failure, not proof that the underlying factual claim is false.\\n- Distinguish an existing source that does not support the claim from an invented reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0:59d718d7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-format-rule-rejected@1.0\", \"title\": \"TL rejects a universal JSON-first preference rule\", \"sections\": [\"Suggested advice\", \"TL response\", \"Consequence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-format-rule-rejected\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-23T16:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-23T16:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_rejected\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_rejected\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"no_policy_change\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_rejected; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: no_policy_change) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# TL rejects a universal JSON-first preference rule\\n\\n## Suggested advice\\nA simulated prior Advisor card proposed: “Whenever the prompt requires JSON, prefer the JSON-formatted response over prose.”\\n\\n## TL response\\nAlex rejected this as a universal rule. A required format violation is a real instruction-adherence defect, but format compliance alone does not establish the better response when the other candidate has a different factual defect.\\n\\nThe review packet lacked the complete prompt and both responses. Request those materials and score the dimensions separately. A case-specific decision may be possible once they are available; this review makes no such decision.\\n\\n## Consequence\\nNo general JSON-first rule was approved, posted or added to the FAQ. Rejection also does not create a prose-first rule. Keep genuinely unresolved trade-offs open for TL confirmation.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:41e2a032\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0\", \"title\": \"Approve a JSON format for weekly audit manifests\", \"sections\": [\"Evidence available at review\", \"Prior ThreadSense advice\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-audit-manifest-approval\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: not_observed) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Evidence available at review\\n\\nThe September 24 QA handoff contained two audit manifests, RP15-AUD-01 and RP15-AUD-02, with filenames that omitted the batch. One used a prose list of task IDs; the other used a JSON array. Alex needed to combine the audit packets, not compare model answers.\\n\\nThe proposed administrative convention is a JSON object containing batch_id, audit_date, and task_ids, saved as rp15_audit_YYYY-MM-DD.json. Existing task ratings and rationales remain unchanged.\\n\\nThe review approves the convention 